      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The name 'Honeoye' comes from the Seneca word ha-ne-a-yah, meaning 'lying finger'.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        23
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Honeoye_Falls%2C_New_York",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Upper Falls area on West Main Street hosts the historic Upper Mill, a four‑story Federal stone building dating to 1827.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17,
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
